<?xml version='1.0'?>
<!--
  Team-supplied ArUco fiducials on the arena's 80/20 fiducial rail.

  The arena provides only the bare rail; the markers and their mounts are the
  team's own kit, attached during setup and removed afterwards (guidebook
  section 4.6.7). These are modelled where the guidebook puts the rail:

    rail        X -2.00 .. -0.50 m, on the inside face of the front wall
    height      Z = 0.40 m, "approximately 40 cm (+/- 2.5 cm) above the
                regolith surface" (section 5.7)
    near end    0.50 m west of the Origin Point, which is the centre of the
                front wall and the origin of the arena frame used throughout
                this world

  Marker centres in ARENA coordinates - this is the table a registration node
  needs, since a detection only helps if you know where the marker is:

    marker    ArUco id    X          Y       Z
    aruco01   0           -1.7125    0.028   0.40
    aruco02   1           -1.2500    0.028   0.40
    aruco03   2           -0.7875    0.028   0.40

  Dictionary is DICT_4X4_50. The marker SQUARE is 0.238 m on a 0.35 m plate -
  the rest is the white quiet zone the detector needs to find the contour.
  Pass 0.238 to estimatePoseSingleMarkers, not 0.35; using the plate size
  scales every translation you recover by 1.47.

  Three 0.35 m plates is what fits: 3 x 0.35 = 1.05 m on a 1.50 m rail leaves
  four 0.1125 m gaps. A fourth plate at this size would leave 2 cm gaps. Drop
  to ~0.25 m if you want more markers for better acquisition coverage.

  All three sit inside the starting zone (X -2.25 .. 0), which section 4.6.7
  requires - fiducials must be completely contained within it.

  Deliberately NO visibility_flags here, unlike lunabotics_zones. These are
  real hardware the camera has to see; the zone outlines are annotations that
  must stay out of perception.

  The textures are generated, not the old ARC ones. Those were recovered from
  git first and turned out to be undecodable: correct binary patterns, but the
  black border ran to the texture edge with no white quiet zone, so no detector
  would ever find them. These are regenerated with a 16% white margin and were
  round-tripped through cv2.aruco.ArucoDetector, which returns ids 0, 1 and 2.

  Regenerate them if your detector uses a different dictionary - scripts to do
  so are three lines of cv2.aruco.generateImageMarker - but keep the quiet zone
  and update the id column above if you change the ids.
-->
<sdf version='1.8'>
  <model name='lunabotics_fiducials'>
    <pose>0 0 0 0 0 0</pose>
    <static>true</static>

    <link name='marker_01'>
      <!-- pitch then yaw turns the plate's face to +Y, i.e. north into the arena -->
      <pose>-1.7125 0.028 0.4 0 1.5708 1.5708</pose>
      <collision name='marker_01_collision'>
        <geometry>
          <box>
            <size>0.35 0.35 0.005</size>
          </box>
        </geometry>
      </collision>
      <visual name='marker_01_visual'>
        <geometry>
          <box>
            <size>0.35 0.35 0.005</size>
          </box>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <pbr>
            <metal>
              <albedo_map>textures/aruco01.png</albedo_map>
            </metal>
          </pbr>
          <ambient>1 1 1 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>1 1 1 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.05 0.05 0.05 1</specular>
          <emissive>0 0 0 1</emissive>
        </material>
      </visual>
    </link>

    <link name='marker_02'>
      <!-- pitch then yaw turns the plate's face to +Y, i.e. north into the arena -->
      <pose>-1.25 0.028 0.4 0 1.5708 1.5708</pose>
      <collision name='marker_02_collision'>
        <geometry>
          <box>
            <size>0.35 0.35 0.005</size>
          </box>
        </geometry>
      </collision>
      <visual name='marker_02_visual'>
        <geometry>
          <box>
            <size>0.35 0.35 0.005</size>
          </box>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <pbr>
            <metal>
              <albedo_map>textures/aruco02.png</albedo_map>
            </metal>
          </pbr>
          <ambient>1 1 1 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>1 1 1 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.05 0.05 0.05 1</specular>
          <emissive>0 0 0 1</emissive>
        </material>
      </visual>
    </link>

    <link name='marker_03'>
      <!-- pitch then yaw turns the plate's face to +Y, i.e. north into the arena -->
      <pose>-0.7875 0.028 0.4 0 1.5708 1.5708</pose>
      <collision name='marker_03_collision'>
        <geometry>
          <box>
            <size>0.35 0.35 0.005</size>
          </box>
        </geometry>
      </collision>
      <visual name='marker_03_visual'>
        <geometry>
          <box>
            <size>0.35 0.35 0.005</size>
          </box>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <pbr>
            <metal>
              <albedo_map>textures/aruco03.png</albedo_map>
            </metal>
          </pbr>
          <ambient>1 1 1 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>1 1 1 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.05 0.05 0.05 1</specular>
          <emissive>0 0 0 1</emissive>
        </material>
      </visual>
    </link>

  </model>
</sdf>
